  "prompt": "Finance asks whether the export's purchase value can be trusted. Check December 2025. On the export side, count the purchase events of the Dublin days 1 to 31 December (by event_date) and add up their value parameter, read from whichever number slot holds it. On the backend side, count the subscriptions whose first payment (their earliest paid_at in payments) falls on those Dublin days, and add up those payments' amount_eur. A first payment that was later refunded still counts on both sides. Return four columns, in this order: export_purchases, backend_first_payments, export_value and backend_value. Return one row. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "export_purchases",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "backend_first_payments",
